id: pm-eqxjzl
title: Expose freshness and completeness of independent dependency advisory feeds before merge
description: The2026-10-20 follow-redirects advisories were visible in OSV and the merged-main Scorecard instance while the registry-backed all-dependency audit still reported zero. The component patch is completed separately; this task owns advisory-source freshness and coverage context before merge. Prefer a project-owned assurance collector or extension on existing SDK primitives rather than ecosystem-specific behavior in the generic SDK.
type: Task
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-20T19:27:47.107Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-20T20:30:44.614Z"
assignee: "harness:codex"
claim_principal: "harness:codex#244d33e51b5f1223152c8358"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "Reuse registered assurance/extension contracts; define bounded queries and explicit provenance for complete project dependency coverage; add a negative control with a lagging zero registry result and positive independent feed, plus unavailable-feed and zero-known-advisory controls; preserve automated updater cooldown and all-severity policy; do not suppress actionable advisories or introduce unbounded polling."
parent: pm-qwoy
risk: medium
confidence: high
expected_result: "A dependency-security decision exposes source/version/time and coverage receipts, detects a fresh authoritative positive result even when another feed returns zero, and distinguishes unavailable evidence from clean evidence."
